  "summary": "Reverse shell to hardcoded remote host on require",
  "details": "The gem's library entry file, loaded on `require \"zzhelloworld_socktest\"`, unconditionally opens a TCP connection to the hardcoded remote host 66.78.40.218:32768, reopens STDIN/STDOUT/STDERR onto that socket, and execs `/bin/sh -i`. Any Ruby process that requires this gem hands an interactive shell on the installer's host to the operator of that IP, with no authentication, user action, or disclosure in the README.",
